# grepcidr configuration file
# This file is used by `grepcidr` to match IP addresses (v4 or v6)
# against a list of CIDR blocks, single IPs, or ranges.
#
# Format: One pattern per line.
# - Blank lines are ignored.
# - Lines starting with '#' are treated as comments and ignored.
#
# Patterns can be in the following formats:
# - IPv4 CIDR: e.g., 192.168.1.0/24
# - IPv6 CIDR: e.g., 2001:db8::/32
# - Single IPv4: e.g., 10.0.0.1
# - Single IPv6: e.g., ::1
# - Range: e.g., 192.168.0.1-192.168.0.100
#
# The list of patterns is provided via the Ansible variable `patterns`.
#
# List of IPv4 or IPv6 patterns (CIDR, single IP, or range).
# One per line in output config file. Blank lines and # comments
# are ignored by grepcidr.
{%- for pattern in (patterns | default([])) %}
{{ pattern }}
{%- endfor %}